amber19sb with Q backbone/charge correction (Best, De Sancho, Mittal,
Biophys. J. 102:1462-1467, 2012). The "Q" correction replaces the partial
charges of ARG, HIP, GLU, ASP and LYS (internal residue variants only) with
those refit to reproduce residue-specific alpha-helix propensities.
All atom types, bonding topology, torsions (and CMAP, where present) of the
underlying amber19sb are unchanged.

Original amber19sb header below:
